carvings~
@@gAnother well-known form of divination was necromancy, the conjuring of the

dead, of which King Saul was culpable when he visited the witch at Endor (1

Sam 28:3-25).  Since divination was closely associated with magic in all it's

forms, biblical writers roundly condemned it (see Lev 19:26,31).

~
