carvings~
@@gLikewise, Hoshea, the last king of the northern kingdom, led Israel away

from God to pursue the worhip of foreign gods and engage in occultic practices.

They set up sacred stones and Asherah poles, they worshiped idols, imitated

the nations around them, worshiped Baal; they sacrificed their sons and their

daughters in the fire, and they practiced divination and sorcery.  The

biblical writer interprets their actions as selling "themselves to do evil in

the eyes of the Lord, provoking him to anger."  As a result, the Lord removed

Israel from his presence (2 Kings 17:7-23)

~
