carvings~
Manasseh, one of the kings of Judah, was guilty in the eyes of the chronicler

for breaking the occult prohibitions of the Torah.  He worshiped the Canaanite

gods, practiced astrology or a form of astral religion ("bowed down to all the

starry host and worshiped them"), "sacrificed his sons in the fire in the

Valley of Ben Hinnom, practiced sorcery, divination, and witchcraft, and

consulted mediums and spiritists" (2 Chron 33:1-6).  The chronicler concludes,

"He did much evil in the eyes of the Lord provoking him to anger."

~
