carvings~
@@gIn a similar way the Isaianic prophecy of the desolation of Babylon

predicts that it will become a haunt for "goat spirits" and other sorts of

demons (Is 13:21).  As in Isaiah 34:14, the Greek Old Testament uses the word

daimonia ("demons") to translate some of the Hebrew words here for wild

animals.  These are a strong connection between wild animals and evil spirits

thoughout antiquity.  The "goat demon" was thought to be in the form of a

shaggy he-goat.

~
