carvings~
@@gIn Ephesians Paul was at pains to point out that people cannot respond to

life's decisions neutrally.  They are deeply affected by a set of evil,

determining influences.  These influences led people on a path that is

directed toward death - life apart from God.  In Ephesians 2:2-3, Paul

described these influences in terms of the environment ("the age of this

world"), an inner inclination toward evil ("the flesh") and a supernaturally

powerful opponent ("the ruler of the kingdom of the air, the spirit").

