carvings~
@@gThe Old Testament also ascribes names to some evil spirits.  Lilith is a

demon who will inhabit Edom after it experiences God's desolating judgement

(IS 34:14).  Although this is the only time Lilith is mentioned in the Old

Testament, she was a well-known evil spirit in Mesopotamia.  She also figured

prominantly in later noncanonical Jewish texts, as, for example, in a Jewish

targum, which records the following prayer: "May the Lord bless you in all your

deeds and protect you from the demons of the night and from anything that

frightens and from demons evening and morning, from evil spirits and phantoms

"

~
